The fresh non-vacuity mutation behaved correctly: for the satisfying input `xs=[]`, changing the required result from `[]` to `[1]` built successfully and failed with `WarnStuckClaimState` on the mismatched heap result. This shows the entry claim is result-constraining, but it does not repair the inconsistent symbolic-enumeration rule. I’m now writing the final seven-stage accounting and evidence-linked verdict.
